gbsharp-emulator
================

This repository is a fork of binjgb by Ben Smith:

    https://github.com/binji/binjgb

Forked from upstream commit c60e138da5a795ebb55e56b11b7e90024e41112c
("BG viewer: Add support for flipped and bank1 tiles (#80)").

binjgb is distributed under the MIT license. That license is reproduced
verbatim in LICENSE and applies to this fork in full. Every copyright header
in the inherited sources is left exactly as upstream wrote it, and every file
added by this fork carries its own header rather than editing someone else's.

    Copyright (c) 2016 Ben Smith

The fork exists to serve GB#, a C# to Game Boy compiler:

    https://github.com/SkyTech6/GBSharp

It adds a stable C ABI (src/gbsharp.h) so that GB# can embed the emulator as
a library, and it builds that library without SDL, OpenGL or imgui in the
link. The emulation itself is upstream's work. Changes made here are listed
one by one in DIVERGENCE.md, each with the reason GB# needs it and whether it
is a candidate to send back.

Any distribution that embeds this runtime, including a game published by GB#,
must carry the MIT attribution above.

Branches
--------

    upstream-main   Upstream's main, fast-forward only. Never commit here.
    main            GB# work. Every commit that is not a merge from
                    upstream-main has a "gbsharp:" subject prefix, so that
                    "git log --oneline upstream-main..main" is exactly the
                    list of things this fork changed.
